TEXT -256 -232 Left 2 !.tran 10m
TEXT -256 -248 Left 2 !.param vfactor = 1 sfactor=1
TEXT -256 -264 Left 2 !.options abstol=1u vntol=1u
TEXT -280 -632 Left 6 ;This example shows the influence of changing the voltage translation factor of all three \ntransformers simultanously. The parameter  l_ is changed according to the higher inductive load of load7\nThe voltage in bus7 is now stabilized and also held nearly constant in the whole range !!!!\nby optimizing the transformer tapings in five different ranges 0-2 2-4 4-6 6-8 and 8-10ms
TEXT -392 -32 Left 5 ;NOTE: All values (voltages,currents,powers) are normalized\n            in this example
TEXT 1128 -304 Left 2 !vs_ s_ 0 1\nvl_ l_ 0 pwl 0s {tap1} 2ms {tap1} 2.5ms {tap2} 4ms {tap2} 4.5ms {tap3} 6.0ms {tap3} 6.5ms {tap4} 8ms {tap4} 8.5ms {tap5}\nvon on 0 1
TEXT 520 472 Left 2 !von1 on1 0 1\nvp p 0 4\nvq q 0 pwl 0s -0.3 10m 1.1
TEXT 776 480 Left 2 !.params tap1opt=0  tap2opt=0 tap3opt=-3 tap4opt=-5 tap5opt=-7\n.param tap1=-1.71992 tap2=-3.99550 tap3=-5.90383 tap4=-7.79690 tap5=-9.51927\nv1 1 0 1\nev7 f 0 VALUE={1e6*IDT( ( v(1)-v(sl7_v))**2)     } tripdv=1 tripdt=1\n.meas TRAN cost FIND v(f) AT 9.99ms
TEXT -320 -280 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
